<topic id = "AENLSB0A9406009002">
<title>
Intermittent wiper relay circuit
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Turn the windshield wiper switch to “INT” position.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect battery positive (+) terminal to terminal “4” and its negative (–) terminal to terminal “6”.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect voltmeter positive lead to terminal “3” and its negative lead to terminal “6”.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that the voltmeter indicates the battery voltage (10 – 14 V).
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect terminal “5” and terminal “4” by a jumper wire.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0A940029.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "134.492mm" ver = "01" gw = "205" gh = "365"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
